{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_x2jsk5cm4asowrcgs3kxbfyfbfqbosjmbxhe5fr6gdztsu3rpzwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four gate conditions hold.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Scope.** The library is one C translation unit (`c_src/src/lib.c`, 176 lines) exporting 7 symbols. `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]` table**, `CMakeLists.txt` has no `option()`/`target_compile_definitions`, and `lib.c` has **no `#if`/`#ifdef` at all** → exactly **one** feature combination. I verified it under **both** cargo profiles, since they generate genuinely different code (and one real bug only reproduced in `release`).\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (all in the crate root):\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 7/7 C symbols exported by the Rust `.so`, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 unresolved non-libc imports. No C file was skipped, so nothing needed translating.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 38 rows, mechanically derived from every guard/`return`/constant in the C.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 34 rows over 8 branch axes × all 7 entry points (not just `maxnmin`).\n\n**Phases B–D.** 54 differential tests, all calling both `.so`s through `libloading` — never Rust directly. Each test `dlopen`s a *uniquely-named copy* of each library, which is the only way to observe `node_count == 0` (the C exports no reset). Results are compared as **raw f64 bits** and `Node` fields are read at **hard-coded C offsets** so a layout change fails loudly. Every `ERRORS.md`/`CONFIGS.md` row is ticked; `./run_all.sh` drives all of it.\n\n### Two real divergences found and fixed (in `src/lib.rs`, never `c_src/`)\n\n1. **Null-pointer death signal.** The Rust dereferenced the caller's `name`/`str` raw pointer directly. With `debug_assertions`, rustc instruments that, so `NULL` gave a non-unwinding panic → **SIGABRT**, while C faults → **SIGSEGV**. Fixed by delegating to libc `strncpy`/`strlen` — literally what the C calls. Caught by out-of-process tests that fork a child and compare the *exact signal*.\n\n2. **`calculate_subtree_sum` NaN payload (release-only).** `sum += child` is one `addsd`, and on x86 the *operand position* decides which NaN survives when both are NaN. gcc makes the recursive result SRC1; LLVM treats `fadd` as commutative and swapped it, returning `0xFFF8…00FF` where C returns `0xFFF8…0000`. Fixed by resolving the tie explicitly rather than trusting codegen.\n\n### Two harness problems I fixed rather than trusted\n- **`cargo test` silently does not rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target** — my first release run tested a stale `.so`. The harness now hard-fails on an artifact older than its source (negative control confirmed it trips).\n- My symbol-parity check wrote to `/tmp`, which is read-only in this sandbox, making the diff **vacuously pass**. Now uses `mktemp -d` and fails if `nm` lists fewer than 7 symbols.\n\n### Adequacy check\nRather than assume the tests bite, I mutation-tested: 15 single-edit mutants injected into `src/lib.rs`. **13/13 non-equivalent mutants caught**; the 2 survivors are *provably equivalent* (`d > INT_MAX` vs `>=` — verified identical over 200k inputs; and the redundant `name[49]='\\0'`, which is dead in the C too). The `maxnmin`/`safe_double_to_int` results are additionally cross-checked against an independent third implementation over 110k+ randomized inputs.\n\n`c_src/` is unmodified (source mtimes unchanged; only the generated `build/` directory was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":209053,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1037,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2b08d0b-89dd-4b08-bf49-a79862f2f16e","uuid":"8a5d1fd4-44f7-4f4e-b9b5-836a4f259b08","timestamp":"2026-08-19T22:15:47.609Z"}
